---
import LessonPage from "../../../components/lesson/LessonPage.astro";
import { defineLesson } from "../../../data/lesson-schema.mjs";
export const page = defineLesson({
  "title": "can for ability and permission · A1 Grammar · Curriculum Map",
  "slug": "can-for-ability-and-permission",
  "level": "A1",
  "topic": "can for ability and permission",
  "category": "Grammar",
  "contentType": "grammar",
  "status": "ready",
  "description": "Say what is possible and ask politely: I can drive , She can’t come , and Can I open the window?",
  "sequence": 5,
  "prerequisites": [],
  "related": [],
  "assessments": [
    "a1-exit"
  ]
});
---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 5</p>
  <h1>Ability and permission with <em>can</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Say what is possible and ask politely: <span class="ex">I can drive</span>, <span class="ex">She can’t come</span>, and <span class="ex">Can I open the window?</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 55–65 min</span>
    <span class="tag">ability and permission</span>
    <span class="tag">polite requests</span>
    <span class="tag">11 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Meet one word with three jobs.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Use can + base verb, always.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Make questions, negatives, and short answers.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Talk about your real skills and rules.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><span class="ex">Can</span> is one small word with three everyday jobs: skills, permission, and friendly requests. You will use it at work, around the city, and at home.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has">has</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have">have</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Do">Do</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Does">Does</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="There is">There is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="There are">There are</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>My sister <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> got two children. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(have got)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Do" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> you work on weekends? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(present simple)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="There is" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a coffee shop on my street. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(there is / there are)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>One driver, one hot room</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"I can drive, but I can’t park downtown. Can I open the window?"</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which part talks about a skill?</li>
      <li>Find the negative form.</li>
      <li>Which sentence asks for permission?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check: choose the pattern</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the whole sentence first. The meaning tells you which form fits.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="can">can</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="can’t">can’t</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Can">Can</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> swim, so I go to the pool every week.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can’t" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> drive at night; his eyes get tired.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Can" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> I open the window? It’s hot in here.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> speak Spanish and English, so she translates for our team.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can’t" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> hear you. The music is very loud.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Can" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> we start the meeting now? Everyone is here.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: one form for every subject</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>With <span class="ex">can</span>, every subject uses the same pattern. The action verb stays in its base form.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>form</th><th>pattern</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>positive</b></td><td>subject + can + base verb</td><td>She can help.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>negative</b></td><td>subject + can’t + base verb</td><td>She can’t stay.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>question</b></td><td>Can + subject + base verb?</td><td>Can she help?</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Short answers: <span class="ex">Yes, I can. / No, she can’t.</span> Do not repeat the action verb in a short answer.</p>
  <p class="note-line">The key rule: <span class="ex">can</span> + base verb for <strong>every</strong> subject. <span class="ex">I can drive, she can drive, they can drive.</span> No <span class="ex">-s</span>, no <span class="ex">do / does</span>, ever.</p>

  <h2>Get to the root: one word, three meanings</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">Can</span> is a <strong>modal verb</strong>. A modal does not name the main action. It adds the speaker’s view of that action. With <span class="ex">can</span>, that view is whether the action is possible: because of a skill, because a rule or person allows it, or because someone agrees to do it for you.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>meaning</th><th>example</th><th>what it says</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>ability</b></td><td>I can swim.</td><td>A skill makes the action possible.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>permission</b></td><td>You can leave early. Can I open the window?</td><td>A rule or a person allows it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>request</b></td><td>Can you help me?</td><td>You ask someone to do something for you.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Context decides the meaning</h3>
  <p>The words alone do not always tell you which meaning is active. The situation does.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>sentence</th><th>likely situation</th><th>meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Can you drive?</td><td>choosing a driver for a trip</td><td>Do you have the ability?</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Can you drive the company car?</td><td>asking about a workplace rule</td><td>Do you have permission?</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Can you drive me to the airport?</td><td>asking a friend for a favor</td><td>Will you do it for me?</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Can is the moving part</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">She can drive. → Can she drive? → She can’t drive.</span></p>
    <p>Only <span class="ex">can</span> moves to the front or becomes negative. The base verb <span class="ex">drive</span> never changes. This is why <span class="ex">Does she can drive?</span> mixes two different systems and is not the target form.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1: ability, permission, or request</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Read the whole situation first. Then choose the chunk that fits.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="can">can</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="can’t">can’t</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Can I">Can I</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Can you">Can you</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>My brother <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> fix computers. He works in IT.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Can you" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> help me with these boxes, please?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Sorry, I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can’t" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> come to the office today. My daughter is sick.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Can I" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> ask you a question about the schedule?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>At this school, students <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> use their phones during the break, but not in class.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can’t" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> find a parking spot downtown in the morning; the streets are full.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Can you" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> call me back after lunch? I’m in a meeting right now.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>My parents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> speak a little English, so we travel together easily.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Permission, requests, and politeness</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">Can I…?</span> is normal and friendly for everyday permission. <span class="ex">Can you…?</span> is often a request, not a question about skill. Tone and <span class="ex">please</span> make the request warmer: <span class="ex">Can you open the window, please?</span> A positive answer to a request is usually <span class="ex">Of course</span> or <span class="ex">Sure</span>, not only <span class="ex">Yes, I can</span>.</p>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>Hear the difference: weak can, strong can’t</h3>
    <p>In a normal positive sentence, <span class="ex">can</span> is weak and quick, and the stress lands on the action: <span class="ex">I can SWIM</span>. In a negative sentence, <span class="ex">can’t</span> is strong and clear: <span class="ex">I CAN’T swim</span>. Listeners often catch the difference from this stress, not from the final <span class="ex">t</span>, so say <span class="ex">can’t</span> with real weight.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2: type the question word or short answer</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Questions start with <b>Can</b>. Short answers end with <b>can</b> or <b>can’t</b>, never the action verb.</p>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Can" aria-label="answer 1" /> you work on Saturdays?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Can" aria-label="answer 2" /> your sister drive?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>No, she <input class="answer-input" data-answer="can’t" aria-label="answer 3" />.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Yes, we <input class="answer-input" data-answer="can" aria-label="answer 4" />.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Can" aria-label="answer 5" /> your parents use a computer?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>No, they <input class="answer-input" data-answer="can’t" aria-label="answer 6" />.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A job ad in the café window</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"Weekend barista wanted. You can choose your hours, and you can learn everything on the job. Staff can’t park behind the café, but you can leave a bike in the yard. Can you start in June? Ask for Dana at the counter."</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You understood can and can’t in a real job ad.">
    <h3>Drill 3: read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="their hours">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. What can new staff choose?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="their hours">their hours</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="their pay">their pay</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="their uniform">their uniform</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="behind the café">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. Where can’t staff park?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="behind the café">behind the café</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="in the yard">in the yard</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="at the counter">at the counter</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="in June">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. When does the café want the new barista to start?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="in June">in June</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="in December">in December</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="next weekend">next weekend</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="can you work on saturdays">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the question</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the question. Remember: can moves in front of the subject.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="work">work</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="saturdays">Saturdays</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="can">Can</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="on">on</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="you">you</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="she can’t come to the meeting">
    <h3>Drill 5: build the negative</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the sentence. Only can’t carries the negative.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="meeting">meeting</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="can’t">can’t</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="she">She</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="to">to</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="come">come</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="cans" data-fix="She can swim very well." data-why="Can never changes. It has no -s form, even after she, he, or it.">
    <h3>Drill 6: one form for every subject</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="she">She</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="cans">cans</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="swim">swim</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="very well">very well.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="do" data-fix="Can you drive?" data-why="Can makes its own questions. Move can in front of the subject and drop do.">
    <h3>Drill 7: can asks its own questions</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="do">Do</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">you</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="can">can</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="drive">drive?</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 8: say it, then reveal</h3>
    <p>Read the cue, say the full sentence aloud, then reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> I can drive. Change to she.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>She can drive.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> They can come on Friday. Make it negative.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>They can’t come on Friday.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> You want to use the meeting room. Ask for permission.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Can I use the meeting room?</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> You need help with two heavy bags. Ask a friend politely.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Can you help me with these bags, please?</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> Can he swim? Answer yes.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Yes, he can.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> Can they stay late tonight? Answer no.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>No, they can’t.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Skills:</b> Say three things you can do well. <span class="ex">I can cook. I can drive. I can read maps.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Not yet:</b> Say three things you can’t do yet. <span class="ex">I can’t play the guitar. I can’t swim very far.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask the teacher:</b> Ask five <span class="ex">Can you…?</span> questions. Listen and give a short answer back. <span class="ex">Can you swim? Can you cook fish?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Permission:</b> Ask four permission questions for your work or class. <span class="ex">Can I leave early on Friday? Can I open a window?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Family match:</b> Compare yourself with someone in your family. <span class="ex">My mother can cook very well, but she can’t drive. I can drive, but I can’t cook.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “After <span class="ex">can</span>, I always use the ______ verb. <span class="ex">Can</span> is the same for ______ subject. For a question, ______ moves in front of the subject. The negative is ______.”</p>
    <p>Then say one ability sentence, one permission question, and one polite request about your real life.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Great. You can talk about ability, ask permission, and make polite requests with can.">
    <h3>Final quiz: can forms and meaning</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="can run">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. He ___ very fast.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="can run">can run</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="cans run">cans run</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="can runs">can runs</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Can I">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. ___ use your phone for a minute? My battery is dead.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Can I">Can I</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I can">I can</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Do I can">Do I can</button></div>
      </div>
